# PERMANENT ARCHITECTURAL & UI CONSTRAINTS

You must strictly follow these UI design laws for every single code generation, refactor, and component creation. Never revert to LLM design defaults.

## 1. BRAND PALETTE (NO AI GRADIENTS)
- ABSOLUTELY BAN all indigo, violet, purple, and neon pink gradients.
- NO floating neon orbs, blurred glassmorphism background glow, or generic dark-mode halos.
- Strict Color System: Use a dedicated, grounded color theme (e.g., deep charcoal, clean slate, dark forest green, or minimalist monochrome, or official PayPal corporate tokens). 
- All custom theme tokens must overwrite untouched framework defaults.

## 2. ICON SYSTEM & TYPOGRAPHY
- DO NOT use generic Lucide icon defaults or basic emojis as UI shortcuts.
- MANDATORY STYLING: Every single icon must utilize a uniform 20px framework, a fixed 1.5px stroke width, and be imported explicitly from the designated icon library (@phosphor-icons/react).
- Avoid cliché metaphors (e.g., no rockets for "launching", no shields for "security"). Use contextual text or custom minimalist line art.
- Prevent wide walls of text. Cap reading widths at 480px for centered copy blocks.

## 3. ANTI-SLOP STRUCTURAL CHECKS
- Reject the generic "AI 3-card grid feature layout" unless explicitly commanded. Break grids up with asymmetrical structures or clean lists.
- Avoid standard white-border boxes on solid dark backgrounds. Use subtle level offsets or distinct background fills instead.

